  "question": {
    "text": "The ratio of vapour densities of two gases at the same temperature is $\\frac{4}{25}$, then the ratio of r.m.s. velocities will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AmFOA",
      "text": "$\\frac{25}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lrs6E",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QKy9R",
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JYCFw",
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{25}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(Vapor density) $=\\left(\\frac{\\text { Molar mass }}{2}\\right)$, I.e, $v d=\\frac{M}{2}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & v_{\\mathrm{rms}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{3 R T}{M}} \\\\ & \\frac{v_2}{v_1}=\\sqrt{\\frac{M_1}{M_2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}}=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
